<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Intentionally empty.

  com.apple.security.app-sandbox was removed: App Sandbox is incompatible with
  being an Accessibility client. ClipySecure pastes by posting a synthetic Cmd-V
  via CGEvent, which is precisely the cross-application control the sandbox
  exists to prevent, so a sandboxed build never appears in System Settings >
  Privacy & Security > Accessibility and auto-paste cannot work. Verified on
  macOS 26: the sandboxed build was absent from that list both from /tmp and
  from /Applications. This is also why the original Clipy is not sandboxed and
  is not distributed on the Mac App Store.

  Do NOT add network entitlements — the app is intentionally offline. Privacy
  guarantees come from field-level AES-GCM encryption and the in-memory FTS
  index, not from the sandbox.
-->
<dict/>
</plist>
